      "rows": [
        [
          "**Frame semantics and semantic-role labeling**",
          "Events and relationships described through their participants: giver, recipient, transferred object, requester, addressee, and so forth",
          "Identify the human relationship before assigning a mathematical interpretation"
        ],
        [
          "**Uniform Meaning Representation and discourse semantics**",
          "Meaning graphs, reference resolution, temporal relationships, and distinctions involving modality across sentences",
          "Preserve who is being discussed, when an event occurs, and whether it happened, was requested, or was merely contemplated"
        ],
        [
          "**Event Calculus**",
          "Formal reasoning about events and the states they initiate or terminate over time",
          "Make changes in location, activity, role, possession, and affiliation computationally inspectable"
        ],
        [
          "**Action-effect models such as ProComp**",
          "Rules connecting actions with preconditions and effects",
          "Translate an action into an explicit account of what it changes"
        ]
      ],
