          "exact_quote": "| Proposed interpretation | Result |\n|--------|--------|\n| The genealogies generate different three-note interval progressions | **Excluded.** Their stage-by-stage pitch relationships agree. |\n| The third entrance creates a distinct sonority in the expanded version | **Excluded as an acoustic claim.** The sonority is identical. |\n| Their historical entrance timing is proportional under a single tempo scaling | **Excluded.** $7:6\\neq27:26$\\. |\n| The expanded version has a smaller full-triad exposure under the sustained-voice model | **Confirmed within that model.** |\n| The expanded performance is musically preferable because it has lower mean roughness | **Not selected.** No accepted criterion establishes that preference. |\n| The figure at the highest-frequency harmonic reference can differ between witnesses | **Retained\\:** Cainan II versus Shelah. |\n",
          "quote_sha256": "3cec0c249f4e487a80bc5f5b099c838c00170a74966e3a5048fb277ab97cd7b9",
