          "exact_quote": "| # | Phoenician | Aramaic / Hebrew | Greek (name) | Latin | Arabic (basic) | Key phonetic / structural difference |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | ʾālep (ox) | 𐡀 / א (Aleph) | Alpha (Α) | A | ʾalif (ا) | Glottal stop → Greek **vowel** /a/; Latin A; Arabic ʾalif |\n| 2 | bêt (house) | 𐡁 / ב (Bet) | Beta (Β) | B | bāʾ (ب) | Stable /b/ across all six |\n| 3 | gîmel (throwstick) | 𐡂 / ג (Gimel) | Gamma (Γ) | C / G | jīm (ج) | Phoenician /g/ → Latin C, later split into C/G; Arabic /dʒ/ |\n| 4 | dālet (door) | 𐡃 / ד (Dalet) | Delta (Δ) | D | dāl (د) | Stable /d/ |\n| 5 | hē (window) | 𐡄 / ה (He) | Epsilon (Ε) | E | hāʾ (ه) | Phoenician /h/ → Greek **vowel** /e/; Latin E; Arabic /h/ |\n| 6 | wāw (hook) | 𐡅 / ו (Vav) | Digamma (Ϝ, later lost) | F | wāw (و) | Phoenician /w/ → Greek /w/ then dropped; Latin F; Arabic /w/ |\n| 7 | zayin (weapon) | 𐡆 / ז (Zayin) | Zeta (Ζ) | Z | zāy (ز) | Stable /z/ |\n| 8 | ḥēt (fence) | 𐡇 / ח (Het) | Eta (Η) | H | ḥāʾ (ح) | Phoenician /ħ/ → Greek **vowel** /ɛː/; Latin H; Arabic /ħ/ |\n| 9 | ṭēt (wheel) | 𐡈 / ט (Tet) | Theta (Θ) | — (no Latin letter) | ṭāʾ (ط) | Emphatic /tˤ/; Greek /tʰ/; Latin had no emphatics |\n| 10 | yōd (hand) | 𐡉 / י (Yod) | Iota (Ι) | I | yāʾ (ي) | Phoenician /j/ → Greek **vowel** /i/; Latin I; Arabic /j/ |\n| 11 | kāp (palm) | 𐡊 / כ (Kaf) | Kappa (Κ) | K | kāf (ك) | Stable /k/ |\n| 12 | lāmed (goad) | 𐡋 / ל (Lamed) | Lambda (Λ) | L | lām (ل) | Stable /l/ |\n| 13 | mēm (water) | 𐡌 / מ (Mem) | Mu (Μ) | M | mīm (م) | Stable /m/ |\n| 14 | nūn (fish) | 𐡍 / נ (Nun) | Nu (Ν) | N | nūn (ن) | Stable /n/ |\n| 15 | sāmek (support) | 𐡎 / ס (Samekh) | Xi (Ξ) | X | sīn (س) | Phoenician /s/ → Greek /ks/; Latin X; Arabic /s/ |\n| 16 | ʿayin (eye) | 𐡏 / ע (Ayin) | Omicron (Ο) | O | ʿayn (ع) | Phoenician /ʕ/ → Greek **vowel** /o/; Latin O; Arabic /ʕ/ |\n| 17 | pē (mouth) | 𐡐 / פ (Pe) | Pi (Π) | P | fāʾ (ف) | Phoenician /p/ → Arabic /f/ (shift); Greek/Latin /p/ |\n| 18 | ṣādē (plant) | 𐡑 / צ (Tsadi) | — (no Greek letter) | — | ṣād (ص) | Emphatic /sˤ/; Greek had no emphatics; Arabic preserves |\n| 19 | qōp (back of head) | 𐡒 / ק (Qof) | Qoppa (Ϙ, later lost) | Q | qāf (ق) | Uvular /q/; Greek dropped it; Latin Q; Arabic preserves |\n| 20 | rēš (head) | 𐡓 / ר (Resh) | Rho (Ρ) | R | rāʾ (ر) | Stable /r/ |\n| 21 | šīn (tooth) | 𐡔 / ש (Shin) | Sigma (Σ) | S | shīn (ش) | Phoenician /ʃ/ → Greek /s/; Latin S; Arabic /ʃ/ |\n| 22 | tāw (mark) | 𐡕 / ת (Tav) | Tau (Τ) | T | tāʾ (ت) | Stable /t/ |\n",
          "quote_sha256": "0a39f9792c7f83179e785f36964e08292d59476e6cd323fc9c56803a6f99a550",
