      "headers": [
        "Repo",
        "Assessment"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`AQARION/φ377-Continuum`, `Eternally-Thriving-Grandmasterism/Ra-Thor`",
          "Sacred geometry modules (Vesica Piscis, Merkaba, Flower of Life, Solfeggio tones) with a \"1048576-dimensional lattice\" and \"Thoth algorithms\". **Unsound.** The dimensional claims are not mathematically meaningful; the Solfeggio frequencies are a 20th-century invention, not ancient. Not usable."
        ],
        [
          "`Hyperstitium/The-Hyperstitium`",
          "A \"recursive myth-field\" and \"digital sanctuary for symbolic protocol\". Poetry and ritual, not computation. **Not a tool.**"
        ],
        [
          "`MIELA-LABS/MPL`",
          "An \"interpreted DSL\" for \"Technomancy\" with \"Solomonic Logic\" and the \"Tesla Protocol (3-6-9)\". **Vaporware.** No evidence of a working interpreter or formal semantics."
        ],
        [
          "`cdli-gh/Cuneiform-OCR`",
          "Legitimate project (Cuneiform Digital Library Initiative) for line/character detection on cuneiform images, but **last pushed 2019** and has 30 stars. Useful only if the Atlas ever needs to OCR cuneiform tablets; currently it does not."
        ],
        [
          "`theseankid/computational-topology`",
          "Persistent homology notebooks. **Generic** — no sacred-geometry or emanation-specific content. `gudhi` or `topopy` already cover this."
        ],
        [
          "`pytop`",
          "A mathematical topology library including embeddings and 3-manifolds. Potentially useful for the W72 embedding question, but `networkx` VF2 is simpler and sufficient."
        ]
      ],
      "occurrences": [
        {
          "source_id": "ec14b911f6564871c5f7c9b031be3d09184015cc076bd0d5395ad84fe9fde015",
