      "headers": [
        "Gap",
        "Tool",
        "What it does",
        "Limitation"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**Cross-script numerical values**",
          "`markomanninen/abnum3`",
          "Gematria for Greek, Hebrew, Coptic, Aramaic, Syriac, Arabic, Phoenician, Brahmi. Additive and multiplicative.",
          "Computes values; does not adjudicate intention."
        ],
        [
          "**Gematria with final-letter conventions**",
          "`KareyPyer/elizabethan-lispies`",
          "Standard and extended final-letter values (ך=500, ם=600, etc.), notarikon, temurah, Atbash/Albam.",
          "Common Lisp; not Python."
        ],
        [
          "**Provenance and reception chains**",
          "`jebboone/deitydb`",
          "4,130 entities, 7,161 relationships, 638 sources, 137 traditions. Reception chains and cross-traditional parallels as query types.",
          "Citation-pointer sourcing, not always verbatim. Check, not authority."
        ],
        [
          "**Exact rational intervals**",
          "`endolith/just_intonation`",
          "`Interval(4,3)`, `.complement`, `.odd_limit`, `Chord(4,5,6).intervals` → `(Interval(5,4), Interval(3,2))`. Pure Python.",
          "Just intonation only; no Chinese lü model."
        ],
        [
          "**Graph embedding / subgraph isomorphism**",
          "`networkx` VF2",
          "`GraphMatcher.subgraph_is_isomorphic`, `subgraph_is_monomorphic`.",
          "Needs incidence data as input."
        ],
        [
          "**Certified UNSAT cores**",
          "`tpt-solutions/tpt-solver`",
          "Trusted checker kernel separate from search; SAT/UNSAT via LRAT/RUP; LRA via Farkas; `--explain` prints implicated constraints.",
          "Younger project; requires `cargo install --path`."
        ],
        [
          "**Cantillation sequence data**",
          "`benemanuel/trop-sequence-finder`",
          "Cantillation mark order across the entire Tanach (Letteris edition), with equivalence-class collapsing.",
          "Sequences, not pitches."
        ],
        [
          "**Virahanka / Sanskrit Fibonacci**",
          "NLTK `virahanka1()`",
          "Computes Sanskrit meter patterns via the Fibonacci recurrence — an independent historical attestation of $0,1,1,2,3,5,8,13$ as a *counting* operation.",
          "Does not connect to Sefer."
        ]
      ],
