    {
      "id": "alignment-table-0ba69615c0825bd1",
      "content_sha256": "0ba69615c0825bd1031d4fc97ade8f5e728fed81cefaf8c16edac91900ef64ff",
      "headers": [
        "Previous confusion",
        "Resolution via TOL"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "\"Only Mars crosses the bridge\"",
          "Mars's fifth stays in-register. The bridge crossings are Yesod→Malkuth transitions, which carry register change"
        ],
        [
          "\"Fire=6/5 requires 5-limit but doesn't prove global tuning\"",
          "Fire is a **node** at a specific register. Its 5-limit value is a node property, not a global tuning property"
        ],
        [
          "\"A–E correction is local\"",
          "A and E are on a specific **path**. Corrections propagate along paths, not globally"
        ],
        [
          "\"80/81 is local vs. global\"",
          "Neither. It is **path-local**: applies to the specific path connecting the two nodes"
        ],
        [
          "\"The elemental set has group structure\"",
          "It does not. TOL is the structure"
        ]
      ],
      "occurrences": [
